# Interactive input

This bashrc runs as the logged-in operator. Do **not** build a repo-wide argv sanitizer.

## Trust model

- Helpers that run user-chosen programs or private keys should validate **foot-guns** (missing/non-executable targets, loose key modes, bad timeouts).
- Prefer `"$cmd" "$@"` / `--args` over string-building. Trusted `eval` of `ssh-agent -s` / fzf / fnm output is OK.
- Do **not** source [`lib/error`](../../lib/error) from bashrc (`die` would kill the shell).

## Required checks

Shared helpers live in [`lib/interactive_input`](../../lib/interactive_input):

| Helper | Used by |
| --- | --- |
| `init_files_bt_program_ok` | `bt` — regular executable file before gdb `--args` |
| `init_files_ssh_timeout_ok` | `cache_ssh -t` |
| `init_files_ssh_key_usable` | `cache_ssh` key path (file; mode without group/other bits; absolute or under `~/.ssh`) |

`bt`: `bt [--] program [args…]` or `bt -p PID` (no mixing). `cache_ssh`: keep TTY + `SSH_ASKPASS_REQUIRE=never` fail-closed for passphrases.
